  <Patch Id="BpOq2iuWmoKVBPIUxpTfKc">
    <Canvas Id="LpHqTzWH7zpLLa16R2kOKa" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="H7IAclMjnBr1ZqOUs8A0cH">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="HrmusbBgAqOAj54JRBEAeS">
        <Canvas Id="TLU6xewGjp44HKTeujwFjD" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="BQC8RMHL1lPoC7MjB4Mt2I" Bounds="-800,-60,660,640" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="ACT IV LAB - Experiment: the globe, stage 2 step 1 - one patch per tile. NOT a shipped unit. Direction: docs/GLOBE-RESEARCH.md.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE QUESTION: can a globe be made of TILES - each tile its own small mesh and its own small texture - instead of one big picture? That is how every real globe works (MapLibre, Mapbox, Cesium), and it is the only road past the 10 km/px ceiling stage 0 showed. This step fixes the zoom at 3: all 64 tiles of the world, no LOD, no view selection yet. If 64 patches meet at their seams, the architecture holds; selecting WHICH tiles comes next and is an algorithm, not wiring.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;FLIP FETCH ON. 64 OpenStreetMap tiles are requested once (about 1 MB; the request carries a User-Agent, as OSM's tile policy asks). TILES READ counts the ones that have arrived. Each one becomes: bytes -&gt; ImageDecoder -&gt; texture -&gt; an emissive material -&gt; a Stride Plane of 8 x 8 cells whose VERTICES are moved onto the sphere by lab/shaders/TileOnSphere_ShaderFX.sdsl: the plane's own texture coordinate is the position inside the tile; tile number + coordinate -&gt; Mercator x,y -&gt; inverse Mercator -&gt; longitude, latitude -&gt; a point on the unit sphere. Inverse Mercator in the VERTEX stage is exactly MapLibre's layout: vertices linear in tile space, so the tile image maps with no distortion.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Before FETCH, the dark sphere underneath is the whole globe. After it, the tiles sit 5 mm above it.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHAT TO LOOK FOR:&#xD;&#xA;- 64 tiles closing without gaps or overlaps along every seam, including the date line (x = 7 meets x = 0);&#xD;&#xA;- continents the right way round inside each tile (mirrored = flip u; upside down = flip v in the shader);&#xD;&#xA;- the two polar rows (y = 0 and y = 7) narrowing toward the poles and the caps left open above 85 degrees - Web Mercator has no poles;&#xD;&#xA;- OSM at zoom 3 is about 20 km per pixel; it is soft on purpose. Resolution is what LOD will buy.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Rules of the lab: no new library surface (every node here shipped already; the shader is a text file beside this document), fetch only on the toggle, results in docs/ACT-IV-LAB.md. Tiles (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL; tile.openstreetmap.org usage policy applies.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="IsY144xe0Tx29w5BWrpU2X" Comment="FETCH" Bounds="60,0,80,30" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="False">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="VACkCf3Z2ckBucPhaqc25f" Comment="TILES READ" Bounds="200,0,100,30" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Integer32" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="VKdtb2Y8r7w0QErhJa75kk" Bounds="320,0,420,45" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="&lt;- FETCH requests the 64 tiles of zoom 3 once, on the up-edge. Nothing is fetched on open. TILES READ climbs to 64 as bodies arrive; each arrival becomes one patch on the sphere.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
